BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Research Seminar in Macroeconomics - Anna Stelzer
DTSTART:20251104T080000Z
DTEND:20251104T093000Z
DTSTAMP:20251202T212446Z
UID:46bnn34qasu4svarbrrpfvd5hf@google.com
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20251006T112422Z
DESCRIPTION:<b><u>Speaker: </u></b>Anna Stelzer<br><br><b><u>Title:</u></b
 > "Are there asymmetries in euro area monetary policy?"<br><br><b><u>Abstr
 act:</u></b><br>We assess a symmetries and non linearities in the dynamic 
 responses of euro area variables in response to monetary policy shocks. Ou
 r multivariate nonparametric mixed-frequency model is estimated using Baye
 sian Additive Regression Trees (BART)\, and we provide comprehensive discu
 ssions of how to compute causal effects in a non linear context. Our datas
 et includes macroeconomic and financial variables  alongside survey-based
  in dicators measuring credit conditions and bank lending transmission cha
 nnels.The results suggest limited effects of expansionary policy shocks wh
 ereas contractionary shocks yield responses in line with theory. There is 
 little variation over the business cycle and in distinct periods such as a
 t the effective lower bound.
LAST-MODIFIED:20251006T112653Z
LOCATION:OMDS-Seminar-Room\, 3rd floor
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
